{
  "name": "How to Plan Your Built-In Shelving Project",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Planning built-in shelving might seem daunting, but it's totally manageable if you break it down. Here's a simple process to get you started. First off, grab your tape measure and get precise measurements of the opening where you want the shelves to go. Don't forget to account for any wall irregularities – walls are rarely perfectly straight! Next, you'll need to locate those wall studs; this is super important for anchoring your unit securely, especially for heavy loads. Before anything is permanent, dry-fit and scribe your unit for a super tight fit against the wall. Once you're happy with the fit, mechanically anchor the unit to the studs. This isn't just about stability; it's about safety. Finally, you can add trim, caulk, and apply the finish work. If this sounds like a lot, or if you're dealing with structural elements, it's often best to bring in a professional. HH Remodeling LLC can handle all these steps, ensuring a beautiful and sturdy result that lasts.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
